7	/**
8	 * The single derived identity of an owner used for duplicate detection.
9	 *
10	 * <p>An owner's {@code identityKey} is
11	 * {@code normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId}, where the
12	 * telephone is its E.164 form, the email is its lower-cased form (empty when absent or
13	 * blank) and the householdId is the owner's shared-household identifier (empty when the
14	 * owner does not share a household). Two owners are duplicates only when their whole
15	 * identity keys are equal — so, for example, two members of the same household (same
16	 * householdId) with different telephones have different keys and are both allowed.
17	 */
